Z||000000||jmw||08-07-2000||04:53 PM||||Hi. I am new to this forum. Am looking for someone in the Birmingham, Alabama area to help me restore my Fiero -- or at least fellow enthusiasts available for consultation. I am tired of being reamed by mechanics, and don't trust them to work on my car anymore. Plus some of what I need is cosmetic, or simple things I just need help getting started on.  I am shopping for parts now, but lack the know-how to install some of them once I find them. I will gladly pay / barter with someone to do what I can't, but want to learn and do as much as I can myself. My private email is jmwhite28@hotmail.com if you'd rather not post. Thanks!||||reg||7
Z||000001||My7Fieros||08-07-2000||05:05 PM||||Well, I USED to live near Birmingham. I've still got family that lives there, and Im going to see them a week from Friday (they're in Vestavia Hills), so if you want I'll stop by and see what you've got! Email me if you want, check out my profile for my email address. <BR>Oh yeah, welcome to the Forum!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||Gold-86SE||08-07-2000||05:06 PM||||<BR>At the risk of sounding contrite, you may not need someone who is geographically close to you, unless that is what you are wanting.<P>The reason that was said is because there are several/many people on this forum who know there stuff and will openly and gladly impart that knowledge to you.<P>First, if you have not done so, purchase these manuals, Haynes and Chilton repair manuals for the Fiero.  Both are good basic information areas and describe many things for you.  Also, as long as you are willing to learn and try, these guys will tell you what you need to know to fix the problem(s).<P>Welcome to the forum and good luck.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Gold-86SE (Fiero Collector)||||reg||1
Z||000003||Carrolles||08-07-2000||05:49 PM||||Hi,<P>I live in Alabaster and would be glad to answer questions and help from time to time.  I have a silver 85SE v-6 4spd.<P>Carroll||||reg||1
Z||000004||DRH||08-07-2000||06:19 PM||||Welcome.<P>I grew up and lived just south of you (Montevallo) until about 15 years ago. I still have family in the area but live in WI now so I don't get in that often. Like gold-86se said though, geography is not always a problem when it comes to advise.<P>One of the 'Fiero Meccas' is up the road from you just north of Huntsville. I stopped by to check it out when I was in the area last month. Ed Parks (the owner) was running errands, so I didn't get to meet him, but I did get to take a look around and sign the Fiero Wall. I can't imagine what part anyone would need that he wouldn't have. I haven't dealt with him directly, but have heard nothing but good things about his parts, his work, and even free advise for Fiero owners. Here's a link to his site:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.angelfire.com/on/fierofactory/start.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.angelfire.com/on/fierofactory/start.html</A> <P>||||reg||1
